@annevk I'll change it back to camelCase... was unaware of that was just matching what the code was doing but all attributes are case insensitive anyways (and the chromium code uses lowercase so was more efficient).

I think defining pattern matching is much more complicated for the UA; typically those are just handed off to a regex match of whether it passes or not. If you define sets of pattern it should look for then you need an API to regex to query what are the supported ranges (which doesn't typically exist in regex engines)

As you see @rlanday was working on auto capitalize but I don't think we have a plan for documenting auto correct. But I believe they are fully independent.
